{
	"Name": "AlertQuery - Okta - User - Authentication - Okta Application SSO from an Unknown Client Device",
	"Description": "A successful SSO into an application where Okta could not identify the client device. Device-based sign-on policy rules cannot evaluate a device they cannot identify, so an unknown client is how a request slips past a rule that would otherwise have stopped it.\n\nEvent type: user.authentication.sso with client.device unknown or absent\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_successful_application_sso_from_unknown_client_device/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/blob/main/rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_successful_application_sso_from_unknown_client_device.toml",
	"GUID": "75c18ec5-3941-5777-ad84-b7a6aa94ce46",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Metadata": {
		"timeframe": null
